      "message": "[error] Line 1668: 🔴 **Callbacks are dropped when IGD validity flips, leaving mappings stuck `IN_PROGRESS`.** `onMappingRequestFailed` returns early on `!igd-\u003eisValid()`, so an in-flight add/renew failure can be ignored if the IGD was marked invalid just before the callback. In that case no state transition to `FAILED/PENDING` happens, retry bookkeeping is skipped, and the mapping may never recover. Keep ownership/source checks (`map-\u003egetIgd() \u003d\u003d igd`) but do not gate failure handling on `igd-\u003eisValid()`: always process the failure for matching in-flight requests, then let existing IGD-update/pruning logic handle gateway health.",
